B.a1b=new A.mk("Step 4 \xb7 Wake-Back-To-Bed","After at least 5 hours of sleep, wake for 10 minutes, set your lucid intention, then return to bed. If you feel depleted the next day, pause this technique\u2014your rest matters more than any lucid win.","Gentle WBTB \xb7 Stretch and sip water")
B.a1c=new A.mk("Step 5 \xb7 In-dream stabilization","When lucidity clicks, breathe slowly. Rub your dream-hands together, look around, touch the ground. Give yourself a gentle goal like \u201cI will stay calm and observe for five breaths.\u201d","Grounding senses \xb7 Small goals")
B.a1d=new A.mk("Step 3 \xb7 MILD intention","If you wake in the night, recall the dream and whisper: \u201cNext time I\u2019m dreaming, I will remember I\u2019m dreaming.\u201d Visualise yourself back in that dream, noticing it\u2019s a dream, then drift off with that intention.","Night affirmations \xb7 Visualization")
B.a1e=new A.mk("Spiritual reassurance","If awareness arrives during a nightmare, call on Allah for protection and command the scene to stop. Nightmares hold no authority over you after waking.","Dhikr \xb7 Protective supplications")
B.a1f=new A.mk("Step 2 \xb7 Reality checks","Pause during the day and do a quick test: count your fingers, reread a sentence, pinch your nose and try to breathe through it. Ask softly, \u201cAm I dreaming?\u201d Repetition plants the habit you\u2019ll need inside the dream.","Reality checks \xb7 Mindful pauses")
B.a1g=new A.mk("Step 1 \xb7 Remember your dreams","When you wake, stay still for 1\u20132 minutes and replay the dream. Write even a sentence. Each small note teaches your brain that dream memories matter.","Morning journaling \xb7 Gentle recall")
